  `aide-prose-end` → `aide-orientation-end`. Keep the existing prose
  body unchanged structurally, but update the prose text to mention all
  FOUR entry-point artifacts (the current text mentions only three —
  coding-playbook/coding-playbook.md, coding-playbook/study-playbook.md,
  research/research.md). Add `coding-playbook/update-playbook.md` to the
  list of entry-point artifacts. Use the exact wording from the design
  doc's "Default Obsidian `orientation` section update" subsection.

- [x] **Insert NEW `aide-config-start` / `aide-config-end` pair**
  immediately after the orientation section and before the playbook
  section. Body content is the prose-driven Obsidian config flow from
  the design doc's "Default Obsidian `config` section content"
  subsection. Includes the argument-shape doc
  (`/aide:brain config [<absolute-path>]`), the 5-step flow (read
  brain.aide → decide target path → edit brain.aide → run sync →
  emit restart message), and the explicit STOP-don't-re-check trap
  warning. The verbatim restart-message text from the design doc
  ("Sync wrote the brain entry. Restart Claude Code so the brain MCP
  server picks up the new entry, then re-run /aide.") goes here.

- [x] **Rename `aide-playbook-start` → `aide-playbook-index-start`** and
  `aide-playbook-end` → `aide-playbook-index-end`. Keep the existing
  playbook body unchanged.

- [x] **Keep `aide-study-playbook-start` / `aide-study-playbook-end`
  unchanged** in name. Keep the existing body unchanged.

- [x] **Insert NEW `aide-update-playbook-start` /
  `aide-update-playbook-end` pair** immediately after the study-playbook
  section and before the research section. Body content is the
  playbook-maintenance methodology from the design doc's "Default
  Obsidian `update-playbook` section content" subsection. The 5 steps:
  identify the change → read the playbook entry-point → apply the
  change with `mcp__brain__patch_note` or `mcp__brain__write_note` →
